ap ␀␀␀␀Catching up ␀␀␀␀/day - pass in ~␀␀␀␀<1␀␀ pulling away␀␀␀Trend: need more data␀␀␀%B␀␀ recap␀␀Not enough data for you yet␀You grew the most!␀␀#␀␀␀ of ␀␀␀␀ for growth␀Top: ␀␀␀ new video, from ␀␀␀ new videos, latest ␀␀␀␀Good morning!␀␀␀%a %d %b␀␀␀␀Biggest growth since yesterday␀␀Still collecting data...␀␀␀␀No new videos in the last day␀␀␀--:--␀␀␀%H:%M␀␀␀%A %d %B␀␀␀␀today␀␀␀admin␀␀␀PIN required␀␀␀␀Updating...␀receiving␀␀␀Can't start: ␀␀␀That isn't an APP-ONLY firmware file.␀␀␀Write failed: ␀␀ KB␀Check failed: ␀␀Upload was interrupted.␀<h3>PIN needed</h3>Use the user name <b>admin</b> and your SubCounter PIN. Forgotten it? Hold BOOT for 3 seconds and clear it in setup mode.␀␀␀␀SubCounter settings - user name: admin, password: your PIN␀␀<h1>Checking&hellip;</h1><p>Looking for a new version on GitHub.</p><script>setTimeout(()=>location.href='/update',5000)</script></div></body></html>␀␀␀text/html␀␀␀You're up to date.␀␀Not checked yet.␀␀␀␀<div style='background:#111;border:1px solid #333;border-radius:12px;padding:14px;margin:12px 0'>␀␀␀<b>From GitHub</b><br>␀␀<span style='color:#30d158'>Version <b>v␀␀␀␀</b> is available.</span>␀␀␀<small>␀<form method='POST' action='/update/github'><button type='submit' style='background:#30d158;margin-top:12px'>Install v␀␀ now</button></form>␀␀␀␀ <small style='display:inline'>(checked ␀␀␀␀)</small>␀␀␀<small style='color:#e62117'>␀␀␀<form method='POST' action='/update/check'><button type='submit' style='background:#2a2a2e;margin-top:10px;font-size:15px;padding:10px'>Check now</button></form>␀␀␀</div><p style='margin-top:18px'><b>Or upload a file</b></p>␀␀␀␀<h1>&#11014; Update firmware</h1><p>Currently running <b>v12.1</b></p>␀␀<h1>&#11014; Update firmware</h1>␀␀␀vtrack␀␀h1_␀h24_␀␀␀␀lastvid␀h ␀␀ days␀␀␀1st hour ␀␀␀% vs usual␀␀1st day ␀␀␀␀% of a typical video␀␀␀␀New video␀␀␀in ␀/hour␀␀␀Heavy rain␀␀Rain␀␀␀␀Clear␀␀␀Partly cloudy␀␀␀Cloudy␀␀Fog␀Drizzle␀Snow␀␀␀␀Showers␀Snow showers␀␀␀␀Thunderstorm␀␀␀␀Â°␀␀Weather␀Set your town on the␀␀␀␀Loading weather...␀␀High ␀␀␀   Low ␀   Feels ␀␀␀Rain likely around %02d:00 (%d%%)␀␀␀Wind ␀␀␀ mph   Sunset ␀␀Next hours␀␀%02d␀␀␀␀%␀␀␀rain chance␀Tomorrow␀␀␀␀  Low ␀␀Rain chance ␀␀␀␀Sunrise ␀␀␀␀Sunset ␀ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/␀␀␀␀==␀␀https://accounts.spotify.com/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=␀␀␀␀&scope=␀user-read-playback-state user-modify-playback-state user-read-currently-playing␀&redirect_uri=␀␀&state=␀   -   ␀Â° ␀ subs␀␀␀Rain around %02d:00␀ available - swipe to Device␀␀␀␀Creators␀␀␀␀Device␀␀  Â·  subcounter.local␀␀Tap an app␀␀Scan to open␀␀␀␀the dashboard␀␀␀No Wi-Fi␀␀␀␀subcounter.local␀␀␀␀Running v12.1␀␀␀Checking...␀ available!␀Up to date␀␀Install v␀␀␀Check for update␀␀␀␀Cache-Control␀␀␀public, max-age=604800␀␀image/svg+xml␀␀␀image/png␀␀␀ checked␀␀␀␀<label><input type='checkbox' name='␀␀␀␀' value='1' style='width:auto'␀␀> ␀␀ selected␀␀␀<select name='␀␀'><option value='-1'␀␀␀␀>Off</option>␀␀␀<option value='␀</select>␀␀␀YouTube␀' onchange='racePv()'><option value='-1'>None</option>␀␀tw␀␀yt␀␀<optgroup label='␀␀␀' data-p='␀␀</optgroup>␀<h2 id='␀␀␀␀</h2>␀␀␀<a href='#firmware'>Firmware</a>␀␀␀␀(saved â€” leave blank to keep)␀AIzaâ€¦␀ open␀␀␀ (saved &#10003;)␀␀␀ (needed for Twitch channels)␀␀␀ minute␀ minutes␀␀␀␀ required␀␀␀Password␀␀␀␀New PIN␀Choose a PIN (4â€“12 characters)␀␀␀␀Leave blank to keep the current PIN␀e.g. 4 digits␀␀␀<h1>&#9654; SubCounter settings</h1><p>Saved on the board only. v12.1␀␀␀ &middot; <a href='/'>&larr; Dashboard</a>␀␀</p><nav class='jump'><a href='#channels'>YouTube</a><a href='#twitch'>Twitch</a><a href='#display'>Display</a><a href='#alerts'>Alerts</a><a href='#phone'>Phone</a><a href='#weather'>Weather</a><a href='#spotify'>Spotify</a><a href='#motion'>Motion</a><a href='#wifi'>Wi-Fi</a><a href='#updates'>Updates</a><a href='#security'>Security</a>␀␀␀␀</nav>␀␀<div style='background:#3a1210;border:1px solid #e62117;border-radius:10px;padding:12px;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:14px'><b>Couldn't connect to Wi-Fi:</b><br>␀<form method='POST' action='/save'>␀<label>YouTube channels (one per line)</label>␀␀<textarea name='channels' autocapitalize='off' autocorrect='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='@yourchannel&#10;@mkbhd&#10;@veritasium'>␀␀</textarea>␀<small>@handles, UCâ€¦ channel IDs or channel links. Put your own channel first â€“ it's highlighted and shown on the night clock.</small>␀␀<label>YouTube Data API key</label>␀<input name='apikey' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' placeholder='␀␀'><small>Only needed if you follow YouTube channels.</small>␀␀␀␀<label>Twitch channels (just the name, one per line)</label>␀␀␀␀<textarea name='twch' autocapitalize='off' autocorrect='off' spellcheck='false' style='min-height:90px' placeholder='shroud&#10;pokimane'>␀␀<small>Type the name as it appears in their Twitch address (twitch.tv/<b>name</b>). Pasting the full link works too. YouTube and Twitch together: up to 10 channels.</small>␀␀␀␀<details␀␀␀␀><summary>Twitch app details␀␀␀␀<small>Create a free app at <a href='https://dev.twitch.tv/console/apps' target='_blank'>dev.twitch.tv/console</a>: Register Your Application &rarr; any unique name &rarr; OAuth Redirect URL <code>https://localhost</code> (any https address works, it isn't used) &rarr; Category: Other &rarr; Client type: Confidential &rarr; Create &rarr; Manage &rarr; copy the Client ID and a <b>New Secret</b>. Your Twitch account needs two-factor sign-in turned on.</small>␀␀␀<label>Client ID</label><input name='twid' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' value='␀␀<label>Client Secret</label><input name='twsec' type='text' class='secret' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='␀Display␀display␀<label>Colour theme</label><select name='theme'>␀␀␀␀</select><small>Accent colour on the board and the dashboard.</small>␀␀␀<label>Screen brightness: <b id='bv'>␀␀␀%</b></label><input type='range' name='bright' min='10' max='100' step='5' value='␀␀' oninput="bv.textContent=this.value+'%'" style='padding:0'>␀␀␀␀<label>Night clock brightness: <b id='nv'>␀␀%</b></label><input type='range' name='nbright' min='1' max='40' value='␀␀␀␀' oninput="nv.textContent=this.value+'%'" style='padding:0'>␀␀␀␀Switch channels automatically every 10 seconds␀␀Estimated live counts between YouTube's rounded steps (â€œest.â€)␀␀<label>Show the big clock after this long without use</label><select name='idleclk'>␀␀␀␀Never␀␀␀</select><small>Touch, press BOOT or pick the board up to go back.</small>␀␀<label>Night clock (dims and shows the time)</label><div class='row'>␀␀␀nightStart␀␀<span>to</span>␀nightEnd␀␀␀␀<label>Subscriber race</label><div class='row'>␀<span>vs</span>␀<div id='rpv' class='rpv'></div><script>const PI={yt:"<svg width='20' height='14' viewBox='0 0 20 14'><rect width='20' height='14' rx='4' fill='#ff0033'/><path d='M8 4v6l5-3z' fill='#fff'/></svg>",tw:"<svg width='16' height='16' viewBox='0 0 16 16'><path d='M2 1h13v9l-4 4H8l-2 2H4v-2H1V4z' fill='#9146ff'/><path d='M7 4h1.5v4H7zM10.5 4H12v4h-1.5z' fill='#fff'/></svg>"};function racePv(){const f=n=>{const o=document.querySelector("select[name="+n+"]").selectedOptions[0];return o&&o.value!='-1'?'<span>'+PI[o.dataset.p]+' '+o.textContent.replace(/</g,'&lt;')+'</span>':'<span style=\'color:#777\'>None</span>'};document.getElementById('rpv').innerHTML=f('raceA')+'<em>vs</em>'+f('raceB')}racePv()</script>␀<small>Swipe down twice from the main count to see it.</small>␀␀Alerts␀␀alerts␀␀Confetti for milestones (bigger milestones, bigger party)␀␀␀Alert when a channel goes live (and switch to it)␀␀␀Daily summary at 9 am (a monthly recap on the 1st)␀␀<small>New-subscriber, overtake and record alerts are always on. Alerts are skipped at night, when the board is face-down, and while Spotify is playing.</small>␀␀␀␀Phone notifications␀phone␀␀␀<small>Get alerts on your phone with the free <b>ntfy</b> app (iPhone and Android, no account needed). Install it, tap <b>+</b>, subscribe to the topic below, then save.</small>␀␀␀subcounter-␀<label>ntfy topic (blank = off)</label><input name='ntfy' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. ␀␀␀␀<small>Anyone who knows the topic name can read it, so make it hard to guess.</small>␀␀␀<details><summary>Own ntfy server (advanced)</summary><label>Server address</label><input name='ntfysrv' autocapitalize='off' value='␀␀␀'></details>␀␀␀␀<button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/ntfy/test' formnovalidate>Send a test notification</button>␀␀␀weather␀<label>Town or city</label><input name='wxtown' value='␀' placeholder='e.g. Glasgow'>␀␀␀<small>Long-press the board's screen and pick Weather. Forecasts from Open-Meteo.</small>␀␀␀spotify␀<p class='ok'>Connected &#10003;</p>␀␀␀␀><summary>Spotify app details (one-time setup, needs Premium)</summary>␀<small>Put the relay page on GitHub Pages (or any https address you own), then at <b>developer.spotify.com/dashboard</b> &rarr; Create app &rarr; add that https address as the Redirect URI &rarr; tick <b>Web API</b> &rarr; Save. Copy the Client ID, Client secret and the same Redirect URI here, and save.</small>␀␀␀␀<label>Redirect URI (exactly as entered at Spotify)</label><input name='spredir' value='␀␀␀␀' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='https://yourname.github.io/spotify-callback/'>␀␀<label>Client ID</label><input name='spid' value='␀␀' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off'>␀␀<label>Client secret</label><input name='spsecret' type='text' class='secret' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='␀␀<a class='btnlink' href='␀␀␀'>Connect Spotify</a><small>Press Agree on Spotify's page and you'll be brought straight back here.</small><details><summary>The relay page showed a code instead?</summary><label>Paste the code or that page's full address</label><input name='url' placeholder='code or full address' autocapitalize='off'><button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/spotify/code' formnovalidate>Use this code</button></details>␀␀<button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/spotify/disconnect' formnovalidate>Disconnect Spotify</button>␀␀␀␀<small>Save the app details first; a <b>Connect Spotify</b> button then appears here.</small>␀␀␀Motion␀␀motion␀␀<small style='color:#e62117'>Motion sensor not detected.</small>␀␀␀␀Shake to refresh␀␀␀␀Face-down turns the screen off␀␀Stand it on its side for a tall leaderboard␀Tall leaderboard is upside down? Tick to flip it␀␀␀␀Double-tap the desk for the next channel␀␀␀␀<label>Desk tap sensitivity</label><select name='tapsens'>␀␀Low (firm knocks)␀␀␀Medium␀␀High (light taps)␀␀␀<label>Calibration</label><small>Put the board in the position you normally use it (on its stand or flat), then press:</small><button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/calibrate' formnovalidate>Set this as the normal position</button>␀␀edit␀␀␀␀Wi-Fi networks␀␀wifi␀␀␀␀<small>The board joins your <b>Preferred</b> network when it's in range, otherwise the strongest saved one. <b>Connect now</b> switches straight away.</small><div class='st' style='margin:10px 0'>␀␀␀␀<label style='margin:4px 0 0'><input type='radio' name='pref' value='-1' style='width:auto'␀<div class='saved'><b>␀␀</b>␀␀␀␀<span style='color:#30d158'>connected</span>␀␀␀␀<button type='submit' formaction='/wifi/connect?n=␀␀' formnovalidate class='mini'>Connect now</button>␀␀<span>fixed IP</span>␀␀␀<label style='margin:0'><input type='radio' name='pref' value='␀' style='width:auto'␀␀␀␀> Preferred</label>␀<a href='/settings?edit=␀␀␀␀#wifi'>Edit</a>␀<label style='margin:0'><input type='checkbox' name='rm␀' value='1' style='width:auto'> Remove</label></div>␀␀␀␀> No preference (strongest signal wins)</label>␀<label>␀Editing: ␀␀␀Add another network (e.g. home)␀Wi-Fi network␀␀␀<button type='button' id='scanBtn' onclick='scan()' class='b2' style='margin-top:6px'>&#128246; Scan for networks</button>␀␀<div id='nets' style='margin:8px 0'></div>␀␀<input id='s' name='ssid' value='␀␀␀' placeholder='Network name (tap one above, or type it)'␀␀␀␀<small>Leave blank if you're not adding a network.</small>␀␀<label>Wi-Fi password</label>␀␀␀<input id='pw' name='pass' type='password' autocomplete='off' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='␀␀␀␀'><small><label style='display:inline;margin:0'><input type='checkbox' style='width:auto' onclick="document.getElementById('pw').type=this.checked?'text':'password'"> Show password</label></small>␀␀␀␀<label>Username (only for work Wi-Fi that asks for one)</label>␀<input name='user' value='␀␀' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='Leave blank for normal Wi-Fi'>␀␀><summary>Advanced settings for this network</summary>␀␀Compatibility mode (Wi-Fi 4 instead of Wi-Fi 6)␀<label>Fixed IP address (blank = automatic)</label>␀<input name='ip' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 192.168.1.250' inputmode='decimal'>␀<label>Gateway (router) address</label>␀<input name='gw' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 192.168.1.1' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀␀<label>Subnet mask</label>␀␀<input name='mask' value='␀␀' placeholder='255.255.255.0' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀<label>DNS server</label>␀␀␀<input name='dns' value='␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 8.8.8.8' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀␀<small>If this one doesn't answer, the board also tries 8.8.8.8.</small>␀␀␀␀Updates␀updates␀Check for updates at start-up (offers to install on the QR screen)␀␀Install new versions from GitHub automatically (at 3 am)␀␀␀␀<small>Either way the board checks once a day and shows when a new version is out; install it from the <a href='/update'>Update page</a>.</small>␀␀␀<details><summary>Update source (advanced)</summary><label>Address of the builds folder</label><input name='updurl' autocapitalize='off' value='␀␀␀␀'><small>Only change this if you build your own copy (a fork) on GitHub.</small></details>␀␀Security␀␀␀␀security␀␀␀␀<p class='ok'>PIN is on &#10003;</p>␀␀␀␀<small>No PIN set: anyone on your Wi-Fi can open this page and change things.</small>␀␀␀</label><input name='pin' type='password' inputmode='numeric' autocomplete='new-password' maxlength='12' placeholder='␀␀<label>Type it again</label><input name='pin2' type='password' inputmode='numeric' autocomplete='new-password' maxlength='12'>␀␀Remove the PIN␀␀nopin␀␀␀<small>After you save, your browser asks for it whenever you open Settings or Update: user name <b>admin</b>, password = your PIN. The dashboard stays open to view. Forgotten it? Hold BOOT for 3 seconds: setup mode doesn't ask for it, so you can change it there.</small>␀␀<div class='savebar'><button type='submit'>Save &amp; restart</button></div>␀␀␀␀</form>␀Firmware␀␀␀␀firmware␀␀␀␀<p style='margin:0'>Running <b>v12.1</b> &middot; <a href='/update'>&#11014; Update</a>␀ &middot; <b style='color:#30d158'>v␀␀␀␀ available</b>␀␀Backup &amp; restore␀␀␀␀backup␀␀<small>Save all your settings to a file, e.g. before a full re-flash or to set up a second board. History and records stay on the board.</small><a class='btnlink' style='background:#2a2a2e' href='/backup'>&#11015; Download settings</a><small><a href='/backup?secrets=1'>Download including passwords, keys and sign-ins</a> â€“ keep that file private.</small><label>Restore from a file</label><input type='file' id='rf' accept='.json'><button type='button' class='b2' onclick='restore()'>Restore &amp; restart</button><small id='rm'></small><script>function restore(){const f=document.getElementById('rf').files[0],m=document.getElementById('rm');if(!f){m.textContent='Choose the .json file first.';return}f.text().then(t=>fetch('/restore',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:t})).then(r=>r.text()).then(t=>{m.textContent=t;setTimeout(()=>location.href='/',12000)}).catch(()=>m.textContent='Restore failed.')}</script>␀␀␀␀<small style='margin-top:16px'>Board Wi-Fi MAC address: ␀␀␀␀</small></div>␀␀<script>scan()</script>␀<h1>␀␀␀␀</h1><p>␀␀␀␀</p><a href='/settings'>Go back</a></div></body></html>␀No update available␀You're already on the newest version.␀␀␀<h1>Installing v␀␀␀␀&hellip;</h1><p>Watch the board's screen. It restarts by itself in about a minute, and this page then goes back to the dashboard.</p><script>setTimeout(()=>location.href='/',75000)</script></div></body></html>␀␀␀No topic␀␀␀␀Type an ntfy topic first.␀␀␀SubCounter test␀Notifications are working! v12.1␀␀␀␀white_check_mark␀␀␀␀Test sent␀␀␀Check your phone in a few seconds. If nothing arrives, make sure the ntfy app is subscribed to <b>␀␀</b>. Don't forget to press Save.␀␀␀Calibrated &#10003;␀This is now the board's normal position.␀␀␀␀Unknown network␀That network isn't saved.␀␀␀Switching to ␀␀␀&hellip;␀␀␀␀The board is leaving this network now, so this page will stop updating. Join <b>␀␀␀␀</b> yourself and use the new address shown on the board's leaderboard. If it can't connect, it goes back to the best network it can find.␀␀Spotify disconnected␀␀␀␀You can connect it again any time.␀␀/debug␀␀/settings␀␀␀/save␀␀␀/calibrate␀␀/api/data␀␀␀/api/history␀␀␀␀/api/csv␀␀␀␀/backup␀/ntfy/test␀␀/restore␀␀␀␀/api/scan␀␀␀/wifi/connect␀␀␀/update␀/update/check␀␀␀/update/github␀␀/spotify/code␀␀␀/spotify/callback␀␀␀/spotify/disconnect␀/favicon.svg␀␀␀␀/favicon.png␀␀␀␀/favicon.ico␀␀␀␀/apple-touch-icon.png␀␀␀/apple-touch-icon-precomposed.png␀␀␀, open␀␀, needs username␀␀␀␀<option value="␀">␀␀ dBm␀␀␀␀)</option>␀␀Joined Wi-Fi but got no IP address (DHCP / device approval?)␀␀␀␀Timed out with no reply from the network␀␀␀␀Network found but its security type isn't supported␀Wrong password (the network rejected it)␀␀␀␀Username or password rejected (work/enterprise Wi-Fi)␀␀␀Network not found (out of range or 5 GHz only?)␀Access point refused the board (MAC filter or client limit?)␀␀␀␀Signal too weak or access point stopped responding␀␀Wi-Fi error ␀␀␀␀ (compat)␀␀␀Connecting...␀␀␀Cancelled with BOOT button␀␀no IP␀␀␀Joined Wi-Fi but got no IP address in both Wi-Fi 6 and compatibility mode. Try a fixed IP in Advanced settings, or allow MAC ␀␀␀ on the router/firewall.␀␀␀␀ saved network␀␀ saved networks␀ | ␀, ␀␀Looking for Wi-Fi...␀␀␀␀None of your saved networks are in ra